# CMS sections contract (admin.plentybg.com)

Content editors (via a separate admin app, `admin.plentybg.com`) can insert
extra sections into gaps between this site's hardcoded sections — never by
editing this repo.

## The mechanism
- `src/lib/sections/anchors.ts` — the anchor registry (every gap between
  hardcoded sections on home/about/contact). Must stay byte-for-byte in
  sync with the same file in the admin app's repo. Never rename or reuse an
  anchor id once shipped.
- `src/lib/sections/client.ts` — `getPageSections(page)` fetches published
  sections from the admin app's public API (`ADMIN_API_URL` env var),
  server-side only, and never throws (returns `{}` on any failure).
- `app/page.tsx` / `app/about/page.tsx` / `app/contact/page.tsx` are async
  Server Components: they call `getPageSections` and pass the result down
  as a `sections` prop into `HomePage` / `AboutPage` / `ContactPage`
  (which are Client Components — they cannot fetch this themselves).
- `src/components/cms/SectionSlot.tsx` — reads `sections[anchorId]` and
  renders each item via `src/components/cms/templates.tsx`, keyed by
  `templateId`. Unknown template ids render nothing, never throw.

## Boundaries
- **Never edit the markup inside any existing `<section>`** in
  `src/components/pages/{home,about,contact}.tsx`. New CMS content is
  inserted *between* hardcoded blocks only, via
  `<SectionSlot anchorId="..." sections={sections} />` — never a raw string
  literal for an anchor id, and never a hardcoded layout at the call site.
- Adding a new template requires a matching renderer in
  `src/components/cms/templates.tsx` keyed by the exact `templateId` used
  in the admin app's `src/lib/sections/templates.ts` — the two repos agree
  only by convention, there's no shared package.
- `ADMIN_API_URL` must be set (`.env.local` for dev, a Vercel env var for
  production) or every `SectionSlot` silently renders nothing.
